 as a probe of ion occupancy and pore structure in the high-conductance Ca<sup>2&#x0002b;</sup>-activated K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>569</fpage>&#x02013;586.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3235974</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Neyton, J., and C. Miller. <year>1988</year>b. Potassium blocks barium permeation through a calcium-activated potassium channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>549</fpage>&#x02013;567.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3235973</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Perozo, E., D.M. Cortes, and L.G. Cuello. <year>1999</year>. Structural rearrangements underlying K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup>-channel activation gating. <source>Science.</source> <volume>285</volume>:<fpage>73</fpage>&#x02013;78.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10390363</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Phillips, L.R., D. Enkvetchakul, and C.G. Nichols. <year>2003</year>. Gating dependence of inner pore access in inward rectifier K<sup>&#x0002b;</sup> channels. <source>Neuron.</source> <volume>37</volume>:<fpage>953</fpage>&#x02013;962.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12670424</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Proks, P., J.F. Antcliff, and F.M. Ashcroft. <year>2003</year>. The ligand-sensitive gate of a potassium channel lies close to the selectivity filter. <source>EMBO Rep.</source> <volume>4</volume>:<fpage>70</fpage>&#x02013;75.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12524524</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Rothberg, B.S., K.S. Shin, P.S. Phale, and G. Yellen. <year>2002</year>. Voltage-controlled gating at the intracellular entrance to a hyperpolarization-activated cation channel. <source>J. Gen. Physiol.</source> <volume>119</volume>:<fpage>83</fpage>&#x02013;91.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11773240</pub-id></citation></ref><r